Usage
-----

### Creating Tables

```sql
CREATE TABLE my_table (
    id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    name TEXT,
    data BYTEA
) USING recno;
```

### Configuration

GUC parameters for RECNO:
- `recno_enable_compression` - Enable/disable compression (default: on)
- `recno_compression_level` - Compression level 1-9 (default: 3)
- `recno_compression_algorithm` - Algorithm preference
- `recno_enable_serializable` - Enable anti-dependency tracking (default: on)
- `recno_max_transactions` - Max concurrent transactions (default: 1000)
- `recno_use_hlc` - Enable Hybrid Logical Clocks (default: on)
- `recno_node_id` - Node identifier for DVV (0-4095, default: 0)
- `recno_max_clock_offset_ms` - Maximum tolerable clock offset in ms (default: 250)
- `recno_uncertainty_wait` - Wait for uncertainty interval to pass before reads (default: on)

